</head>
<body dir=3D"ltr">
<div style=3D"direction: ltr; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em; font-fam=
ily: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontService, Calibri, Helvetica, sa=
ns-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);" class=3D"elementToProof">
Thank you for correcting the closure. Your office wrote: &quot;This was an =
error. There was boilerplate language in the template I was using and I neg=
lected to delete the language that was not applicable to this request.&quot=
; The request is open. That matter is closed
 between us.</div>
<div style=3D"direction: ltr; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em; font-fam=
ily: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontService, Calibri, Helvetica, sa=
ns-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);" class=3D"elementToProof">
The fee waiver is not. Your office answered my request for the basis of the=
 denial by quoting ORS 192.324(5) and then stating: &quot;Lane County has r=
eviewed your request for a fee waiver and has concluded that the disclosure=
 of the records you have requested would
 not primarily benefit the general public.&quot;</div>
<div style=3D"direction: ltr; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em; font-fam=
ily: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontService, Calibri, Helvetica, sa=
ns-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);" class=3D"elementToProof">
That is the statute followed by the conclusion. Between them there is nothi=
ng. A custodian's denial must be reasonable under the totality of the circu=
mstances, and a denial that identifies no circumstance, weighs no factor, a=
nd engages no part of the showing
 it solicited cannot be evaluated by anyone, including a reviewer. In Defen=
se of Animals v. Oregon Health Sciences University, 199 Or App 160 (2005).<=
/div>
<div style=3D"direction: ltr; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em; font-fam=
ily: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontService, Calibri, Helvetica, sa=
ns-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);" class=3D"elementToProof">
Your office set the standard it would apply. Your questionnaire states that=
 Lane County &quot;considers all factors set out in the Attorney General's =
Public Records and Meetings Manual and relevant legal authorities,&quot; an=
d names four: the time, expense, and interference
 with regular business; the volume of records; the necessity to segregate e=
xempt from non-exempt material; and the extent to which the records do not =
further the public interest.</div>
<div style=3D"direction: ltr; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em; font-fam=
ily: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontService, Calibri, Helvetica, sa=
ns-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);" class=3D"elementToProof">
Not one of those four has been named in either denial. I addressed all of t=
hem on September 23, and I addressed the Manual's factors besides. Your off=
ice's own figures answer three of them: the expense is $71.91 by your estim=
ate, the volume is two categories
 scoped in your own spreadsheet, and the segregation burden is the one your=
 office carried when it reviewed and released the item 8 records at no char=
ge in four minutes. The fourth, the public interest, is the one your office=
 is required to weigh, and it has
 instead been announced.</div>
<div style=3D"direction: ltr; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em; font-fam=
ily: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontService, Calibri, Helvetica, sa=
ns-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);" class=3D"elementToProof">
I will state the ground again, since it has not been answered. On March 27,=
 2026, at 11:04 AM, a United States Forest Service special agent emailed a =
Lane County deputy, subject &quot;Siltcoos WC Volunteer,&quot; copying two =
Oregon State Police detectives, and transmitted
 my name, my date of birth, my driver's license number, my residence, my wo=
rk schedule, my duties, my correspondence, and my text messages, with a com=
mitment to &quot;keep you up to date.&quot;=B9 The state's own file conclud=
es there is no evidence I committed any crime.=B9
 Items 1 and 2 are the record of what your office did with that transmissio=
n. Whether a county sheriff's office circulates, acts on, or retains a citi=
zen's personal file sent to it without a crime is not a private curiosity. =
It is the conduct of a public body,
 and it is the reason the statute exists.</div>
<div style=3D"direction: ltr; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em; font-fam=
ily: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontService, Calibri, Helvetica, sa=
ns-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);" class=3D"elementToProof">
The archive at oprdvolunteerabuse.org publishes the records of eight state =
and federal institutions in this matter at permanent public addresses, and =
it already carries this county's correspondence. Records produced under thi=
s request will be public within
 days. There is no commercial purpose and no advertising.</div>
<div style=3D"direction: ltr; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em; font-fam=
ily: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontService, Calibri, Helvetica, sa=
ns-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);" class=3D"elementToProof">
Name the factor. State which of the four your office relies on, and how it =
was weighed against the public interest in the records, so that the denial =
is a decision under ORS 192.324(5) rather than an announcement. Until then =
the denial stands unexplained, and
 this letter stands with it on the public record.</div>
<div style=3D"direction: ltr; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em; font-fam=
ily: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontService, Calibri, Helvetica, sa=
ns-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);" class=3D"elementToProof">
Respectfully,</div>
<div style=3D"direction: ltr; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em; font-fam=
ily: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontService, Calibri, Helvetica, sa=
ns-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);" class=3D"elementToProof">
Robert Samuel White</div>
<div style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontService, =
Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">
<br>
</div>
